    rdfs:label "Evidence for Morphia used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. OPIUM"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The meconic acid associated with this salifiable base has no narcotic power by itself, but may probably promote the activity of the morphia.” Opian or narcotine, and morphia, may be well prepared by the following process."@en ;
